ding a Marginal Probability Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ce2c47a-ee13-507c-a79d-857b7af231e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.75$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270492} {:answer/id #uuid "8f0c53ee-16d3-58cb-8669-969e63371e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.55$ | $0.4$ | $0.05$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270512} {:answer/id #uuid "9780a289-0f1c-58c7-9565-ca1c5b0712b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270601} {:answer/id #uuid "d0fcf979-9a70-5d9d-bbb9-bd39664412bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.55$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271107} {:answer/id #uuid "fb0f2ae1-f251-5e67-8057-21094da5bcf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.35$ | $0.35$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0fcf979-9a70-5d9d-bbb9-bd39664412bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.55$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271107} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ddab9aa-df66-5eb8-9528-30e81047e11d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "99d065a3-9932-5ffa-a58b-7761ca7b17a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-142833" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find the marginal mass function for $X.$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.4$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, the marginal mass function for $X$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.55$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272378 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110666 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7640012b-79f9-5f6b-a26b-a7f4fe8c0e7b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Secant-Tangent Identity: Replacing a Squared Secant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2126811f-3b88-5a05-8d43-1c3d5a25748d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269550} {:answer/id #uuid "245b36c0-1e9b-57d0-9e2d-fc22550ca369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269587} {:answer/id #uuid "47859517-03d4-5347-b3fc-8eb75caf4a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269918} {:answer/id #uuid "588d09e2-68fa-54ff-bf72-7d34fe995945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270050} {:answer/id #uuid "68e67ac2-4980-5f8d-a7d2-7bf6639ac014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2126811f-3b88-5a05-8d43-1c3d5a25748d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269550} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f999d6d-ac4b-5c87-8b1f-35a5c4564bbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbc5e1b2-87c4-5246-9d7e-ecb257cc934a" :question/math-academy-id "q-142835" :question/problem "$\\frac{2{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\,{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{2\\,(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+2{tan}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}}{\\cancel{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{1+2{tan}^{2}⁡x}=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110666 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7640012b-79f9-5f6b-a26b-a7f4fe8c0e7b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Secant-Tangent Identity: Replacing a Squared Secant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "304dde44-20c4-5678-a462-a143bc700873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269703} {:answer/id #uuid "5f4d7ccb-6a93-5802-9236-ce06491ed8c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270113} {:answer/id #uuid "a402cd41-72cf-556c-91b9-7acf338994ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270734} {:answer/id #uuid "c912289d-9629-527c-9f02-70c6112b4b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271034} {:answer/id #uuid "fb01e43c-7b1f-5d18-ad5c-c9badf476f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f4d7ccb-6a93-5802-9236-ce06491ed8c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270113} :answer-field/id #uuid "fea27859-5aac-55b2-ac2f-7db0b1bf734f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7824f8f-c1b4-50c2-a8cc-85b1111053c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-142839" :question/problem "$\\frac{1-{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =\\frac{1-(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110665 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91100afb-9a36-57c0-9f30-4692cfef0b93" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Secant-Tangent and Other Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53a1afef-ab20-5945-b76e-734ddce1d287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+2{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270013} {:answer/id #uuid "640b4baa-bd5a-5438-8ead-3ad792f8ca79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270156} {:answer/id #uuid "9f59147e-3b45-5292-abf8-9bd74860dab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270682} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc3cba1-26e2-5c14-abf1-4ce11a76db7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271204} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d608dc-7308-59e2-ad6e-96afa80f19bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "640b4baa-bd5a-5438-8ead-3ad792f8ca79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270156} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb5b09ad-bc1f-512d-8096-60f9e316d665" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc757669-b204-5044-83d4-679ef2bca4ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-142871" :question/problem "${cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,({sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe rewrite the given expression using the secant-tangent identity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,({sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x) & ={cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\,{cos}^{2}⁡x=1-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the above identities, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}⁡x}} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x\\text{ }\\,({sec}^{2}⁡x-2{tan}^{2}⁡x)=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363245 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87675618-337f-5af2-8ad7-9132c080785a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4999140-0d13-559f-82aa-04866874811c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363247} {:answer/id #uuid "7a3e430b-d923-5296-a7ca-989631c7e330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363248} {:answer/id #uuid "80729c9c-5883-5ad9-9c8c-9b30b4df7eba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363249} {:answer/id #uuid "2077f734-6970-5b4d-a64f-8002e8ee0701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363250} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd952fb-a20a-50c5-b031-7432fb3653ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4999140-0d13-559f-82aa-04866874811c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363247} :answer-field/id #uuid "37e1e6b6-7d76-5dc6-b274-7c6f617f4cd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "753f9054-4350-51a9-85ca-8852ab3b386a" :question/math-academy-id "q-142874" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=3\\,|\\,Y=2)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\nP(X=3\\,|\\,Y=2)=\\frac{P(X=3,Y=2)}{P(Y=2)}=\\frac{f(3,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(2) & =f(1,2)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(3,2)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting ${f}_{Y}(2)=\\frac{3}{4}$ and $f(3,2)=\\frac{1}{2}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(3,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87675618-337f-5af2-8ad7-9132c080785a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91982de6-25e6-5cdc-94cb-52df924aab1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363254} {:answer/id #uuid "debf5643-703c-528d-809f-57f122ae89d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363255} {:answer/id #uuid "7d60d4fa-e3ad-5785-8b24-86c0fd909650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.71" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363256} {:answer/id #uuid "477d48da-ef19-5da0-b7a7-ae00b777f320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363257} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c4387a-63b2-5706-b96e-f83e13111f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91982de6-25e6-5cdc-94cb-52df924aab1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363254} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aee25f9-f0a2-551e-b27d-d17636ddbe1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363253}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eed29b47-02f5-5155-b8d3-8b5211613903" :question/math-academy-id "q-142876" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=2\\,|\\,Y=2)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\nP(X=2\\,|\\,Y=2)=\\frac{P(X=2,Y=2)}{P(Y=2)}=\\frac{f(2,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(2) & =f(1,2)+f(2,2) \\\\  & =0.25+0.1 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(2,2)=0.1.$ \n\nFinally, substituting ${f}_{Y}(2)=0.35$ and $f(2,2)=0.1$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(2,2)}{{f}_{Y}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1}{0.35} \\\\  & ≈0.29.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363301 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "348dfcb8-2325-5929-b622-5423b7e37a53" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability Over an Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23ee24bb-0bcf-53b1-8615-0b40b2a5d01c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363303} {:answer/id #uuid "292ff05f-e3db-5cb3-84fc-f5042710407a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363304} {:answer/id #uuid "2405270c-8f82-548a-af3b-c5f80233bd66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363305} {:answer/id #uuid "57b8b6b1-bc80-5a30-9efc-cd453873debe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363306} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc5e80d-11b9-542c-bc46-b1e3071fe873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "292ff05f-e3db-5cb3-84fc-f5042710407a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363304} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6c873c8-8a75-526b-947f-b726e9125062" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363302}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "747c65d8-31c2-5925-9aa8-b6c78ed4bae5" :question/math-academy-id "q-142899" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0$ |\n\nCompute $P(2<Y\\le 6\\,|\\,X=0)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<Y\\le 6\\,|\\,X=0) & =\\frac{P((2<Y\\le 6),X=0)}{P(X=0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=0,(2<Y\\le 6))}{P(X=0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=0,Y=4)+P(X=0,Y=6)}{P(X=0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0,4)+f(0,6)}{{f}_{X}(0)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(0) & =f(0,0)+f(0,2)+f(0,4)+f(0,6) \\\\  & =0.25+0.05+0.1+0 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(0,4)=0.1$ and $f(0,6)=0.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<Y\\le 6\\,|\\,X=0) & =\\frac{f(0,4)+f(0,6)}{{f}_{X}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1+0}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1}{0.4} \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
